{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller","id":1074562,"title":"New mage storyteller","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-07T02:16:18-07:00","id":1074562,"title":"New mage storyteller","content":"Hello there ! So here's the deal, I want to run a mage chronicle for my regular player group. Now i have some experience storytelling Vampire the requiem, and even though i'm more familiar with mage the ascension, i was digging the second edition of requiem and the chronicle of darkness so much that i bought Mtaw 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> And WOW, this game is confusing, especially the cosmology. I'm digging the gnostic feeling of the game and the occult mysteries but well, i find it difficult to warp my head around the mage cosmology, The supernal realms are just diffirent vision of the same place but you can summon different entities from it ? Do they have self-awereness ? Do they interact with each orther ? What about bounds ? are they just concepts made flesh ? Is the supernal realms another world all together or just an idea ? and what about the abyss ? The abyss seems like a very real (bad) place fulll of nasty thing and even nastier realities. So yeah, as you can see i have a loooooot of questions, the universe is huge and i love it but i can't quite comprehend it just yet. <br /> <br /> So any help/advice would be appreciated. There is no plot for the chronicle just yet, heck i'm still considering going Ascenscion over Awakening.<br /> <br /> (I apologize in advance for my poor english, it's not my primary language)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T02:51:36-07:00","id":1074569,"title":"","content":"It's kind of supposed to be confusing, every question you raise can become a potential plot hook or setting detail that you can customize to your personal preferences.<br /> <br /> The Supernal Realms are more like a layer of reality than a place, Mages just describe them in their most abstract form as places because it's easier to wrap your head around than the actual 11th dimension approach. It's indeed multifaceted on top of that, and the five &quot;realms&quot; that Mages draw from aren't even the whole of it. Just as the Abyss has everything not possible or untrue in it so to does the Supernal have everything that is, and there's a lot more of it than can be captured in the five Paths. <br /> <br /> Do they interact with each other? Not really, because the Path is a filter for viewing the Supernal, and usually (Without Prime 4 Apocalypse) no one is using two different filters at the same time. What happens when you are though? Plot.<br /> <br /> Stopping here, got work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T06:14:33-07:00","id":1075446,"title":"","content":"I see, well, thank you for your clarifications<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T08:07:23-07:00","id":1075483,"title":"","content":"Gonna take my own stab at answering it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The supernal realms are just diffirent vision of the same place but you can summon different entities from it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Mrm said, the Supernal is not a &quot;place&quot;, but more like an aspect of reality. It represents and underpins reality as a whole, but it's not a place you can walk to. The Realms themselves may or may not be &quot;real&quot; in a strict sense; different cultural traditions hold different ideas. The Tremere believe the divisions exist but are forced and arbitrary; produced by the mythic Dragons of Atlantis, along with the Watchtowers. The Mages of Mutapa seem to see it otherwise; each Path being a lineage from a divine ancestor, but all Awakened drawing from the same unified source.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Paths are best thought of as perspectives, though, rather than as a union with a specific place that other Mages can't access. Because, again, not a &quot;place&quot; in a physical sense.<br /> <br /> Supernal entities may be creatures, or they might actually just be what happens when you give a concept influence locally over reality. No different from how putting enough heat into wood starts a fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they have self-awereness ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most appear to. They can quite often talk and communicate in a very human manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they interact with each orther ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unknown and up for debate. Certainly, they seem to, on some level. They're aware of each other, at the very least. If asked about the Supernal, these entities will have knowledge of, and mention, the Exarchs, even if totally unrelated or outright opposed to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about bounds ? are they just concepts made flesh ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bound are a Mystery. Whatever else they may be, they're manavoric entities which use the Arcanum; feasting on souls and worship. The Atlantean paradigm sees the Bound as the Old Gods; the formerly Supernal entities, cast out beyond their former station when the Exarchs sat the Thrones and claimed the Supernal as their own. Whether that's the case or not is up to you, but there's an entire set of Archmasters whose big goal is to restore one of the Bound to the Supernal and ride its coat tails up into the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Man, that's a lot of capital letters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the supernal realms another world all together or just an idea ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't explicitly answered, but it definitely isn't a place you can walk to. Archmasters can, briefly, force their perspective on the Supernal to make places within it, but the Supernal itself is... Something else. Does the law of gravity reside anywhere? Does the meaning found in art have a physical location?<br /> <br /> (And, no, don't say in serotonin and dopamine levels. Smartass.)<br /> <br /> The Supernal is a part of reality. It gives reality its form and function. Importantly, it also imparts reality its meaning and order.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it's up to Mages to figure out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what about the abyss ? The abyss seems like a very real (bad) place fulll of nasty thing and even nastier realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is to the Supernal as a shadow is to light; it is the Supernal's antithesis. It isn't malefic evil, as it was largely first conceived to be in 1e, but it is definitely inimical to all sane, sensible, and reasonable minds. It's every impossibility gathered in one non-place; an infinite array of still-born godlings that are universes unto themselves, all trying to force their way into reality and remake it in their own image. The Abyss is corrosive and destructive and ultimately rejected by the Fallen World, sometimes violently, as a body rejects an invading virus.<br /> <br /> The Abyss is what stands between the mundane and the Truth; eternally blocking clear sighted vision with impossible possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T10:14:08-07:00","id":1075513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The supernal realms are just diffirent vision of the same place but you can summon different entities from it ? Do they have self-awereness ? Do they interact with each orther ? What about bounds ? are they just concepts made flesh ? Is the supernal realms another world all together or just an idea ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I think of the relationship between the Supernal World and the Fallen (or Phenomenal) World is that the Fallen is reality and the Phenomenal is the truth that defines it. For a rough analogy from popular media, the Supernal is to the Phenomenal as the code is to the Matrix. The various Supernal Realms are like categories of those truths. Pandemonium, for example, is the totality of the symbols that define Mind and Space within the Phenomenal World. Some of these symbols do indeed appear to display autonomy and self-awareness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller#post1074562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what about the abyss ? The abyss seems like a very real (bad) place fulll of nasty thing and even nastier realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Supernal is truth, then the Abyss is untruth, and in the same way that the Supernal defines the Phenomenal, the Abyss defines Paradox - the unreality to the Abyss's Untruth. In the Matrix analogy, the Abyss would be like corrupted code. It is no more a place than the Supernal Realms are, but its corruption can bring unreal things into Phenomenal reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:04:50-07:00","id":1075592,"title":"","content":"Some of your issues with Mage 2E are caused by the tight restrictions the developers had on word-count. You can infer some of what the others have said from the Core, but a lot of the people speaking above have read 1E books that clarified a lot of the same questions we would have been asking if we started on 2E before 1E too. So no biggie.<br /> <br /> They've answered your questions pretty well, so I'll add something else that may not be immediately apparent. Ascension has the setting established pretty thoroughly from what I am guessing----but Chronicles of Darkness practically <i>begs</i> for you to fill in the gaps yourself, and so, it <i>deliberately </i>leaves gaps for you, the ST, to fill.<br /> <br /> These games drop all kinds of stuff everywhere between 1E and 2E books that make things seem more interconnected than they initially display themselves, but not to give ST's hints of some greater meta-plot for you to figure out and adhere to, but more that it wants to give you more legos to build your own setting out of. Is Arcadia the same as the Changelings? How come Strix from Requiem can mess with the God-Machine? This is all for you to figure out.<br /> <br /> You can even just flat-out choose to ignore aspects of the setting(s) if it will make your story better for your players, as long as they sorta know in advance that what you are doing will deviate from the books so they don't get upset. For example, Mage establishes the Lower Depths as <i>definitely</i> separate from the Abyss, but I prefer to make them a lot more inter-related than the books say.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Mage cosmology is definitely the harder of the cosmologies, half because it doesn't play nice with the other game cosmologies, and because when you ignore all the power-gaming you can do in Mage, the game is really about philosophy and perspective. Instead of a huge wealth of paradigms, though, the Mage 2E game assumes that most people naturally come to 5 &quot;paradigms&quot; as a matter of course--the Paths are like archetypes that Awakened Mages just naturally fall into. They stop having those Paths per se when they reach Archmastery and strike their own path, which could be very loosely analogous to Ascensions paradigms, which would I guess sorta make sense if I'm not fully off the mark, given that archmasters participate in practically their own game---the ascension war.<br /> <br /> Either way, we have a space arcanum and a mind arcanum that already says that space and mind are illusions of our perspective, so the Supernal Realms wouldn't be the Supernal Realms unless they embodied that too. It is less important to be accurate over what the books say something definitely is concerning psychoactive places like the Hedge or the Supernal Realms, and focus more on eliciting an interesting response from your players--play with their perspectives, emphasis theme over detail, make them feel like they've learned something while also having more questions so that they keep coming back for <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> Since Mage is a game about being addicted to mysteries, your job as ST will be to get your players addicted to the mysteries. Which is great---it means you do not need to answer all of your own questions right away either!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:19:46-07:00","id":1075602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075592#post1075592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Arcadia the same as the Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for this one specifically, the answer is explicitly no, at least in 2e. In 1e it was teased at a lot and left for the ST to decide if they wanted to, but in 2e they decided to stop beating around the bush and just tell us. Changeling Arcadia and Mage Arcadia cannot be the same place, because Mage Arcadia is not a place at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:21:21-07:00","id":1075619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075602#post1075602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for this one specifically, the answer is explicitly no, at least in 2e. In 1e it was teased at a lot and left for the ST to decide if they wanted to, but in 2e they decided to stop beating around the bush and just tell us. Changeling Arcadia and Mage Arcadia cannot be the same place, because Mage Arcadia is not a place at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was this said? Is it in a book or is it from like a blog or forum post?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:30:32-07:00","id":1075624,"title":"","content":"It's been said on this forum about a half-dozen times now, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:42:22-07:00","id":1075626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075619#post1075619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where was this said? Is it in a book or is it from like a blog or forum post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try searching for Dave Brookshaw's posts, in this or other forums. The long-standing Arcadia Question has finally been answered with a big No. And even without external confirmation, we can infer that they can't be the same, since one is an incorporeal concept (to the dismay of mages) and the other is an all-too corporeal place (to the dismay of changelings).<br /> <br /> However, even if the two aren't the same, the phenomena and entities in the Land of Faerie still resonate strongly with concepts that are the Kingdom of Enchantments. I've seen interpreting Changeling!Arcadia as a huge Emanation connected to Mage!Arcadia, or at least a realm housing a huge Arcadian Emanation, and it kinda makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:47:51-07:00","id":1075628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075626#post1075626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try searching for Dave Brookshaw's posts, in this or other forums. The long-standing Arcadia Question has finally been answered with a big No. And even without external confirmation, we can infer that they can't be the same, since one is an incorporeal concept (to the dismay of mages) and the other is an all-too corporeal place (to the dismay of changelings).<br /> <br /> However, even if the two aren't the same, the phenomena and entities in the Land of Faerie still resonate strongly with concepts that are the Kingdom of Enchantments. I've seen interpreting Changeling!Arcadia as a huge Emanation connected to Mage!Arcadia, or at least a realm housing a huge Arcadian Emanation, and it kinda makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm just a bitch but I do kind of prefer stuff that makes it to print, but I understand that the devs are constantly refining on what their predecessors have built. I just always found it more fascinating for the Arcadia's to be linked or one and the same. I do like the Emanation realm thing though. Mostly, I just like the idea that the realms of Faerie are places even Archmages should think twice before interfering with (I know I know that's a minority position for a mage player, but whatever...), and I kind of always thought Time and Fate would make excellent Archigenitors, so I personally loved the idea of the two Arcadias being the same because it gave me an excuse to say that Ruin and Prophet cannot find traction to be Archigenitors because of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Thanks for answering my questions you two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:55:10-07:00","id":1075631,"title":"","content":"Edit: Disregard. Reading comprehension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:04:55-07:00","id":1075633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075628#post1075628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm just a bitch but I do kind of prefer stuff that makes it to print, but I understand that the devs are constantly refining on what their predecessors have built. I just always found it more fascinating for the Arcadia's to be linked or one and the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it was explicitly answered in Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:05:57-07:00","id":1075634,"title":"","content":"The Ruin is about nihilism; making people think they can't pursue opportunities in front of them, out of cynicism borne of too many failures and suffering.<br /> The Prophet is about elitism; making people think that history can only be shaped by great leaders separate from the masses.<br /> <br /> The existence and doings of the True Fae seem to promote both of those concepts. They're majestic god-like beings who deny your life and steal your destiny from you. Which is why I think that Changeling!Arcadia is where the Ruin and the Prophet hold dominion.<br /> <br /> Now, this doesn't mean the True Fae are servants of the Exarchs, not any more than every clergy of established religions being servants of the Father. The relation between the Fallen and the Supernal is more than simple causality. But still, this would indeed make even archmages think twice about messing with the Gentry and their homeland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:08:50-07:00","id":1075636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075628#post1075628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm just a bitch but I do kind of prefer stuff that makes it to print, but I understand that the devs are constantly refining on what their predecessors have built. I just always found it more fascinating for the Arcadia's to be linked or one and the same. I do like the Emanation realm thing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not a bitch. It's perfectly reasonable to go by what's printed and to disregard word-of-author. In this case, though, I don't think word-of-author is needed to establish that the two Arcadias cannot be the same. One is a place where stories are sentient and the other is a collection of symbols and concepts related to fate and time. They can certainly be connected, the emanation realm idea being one example of how that might work, bur Changeling Arcadia is definitely a place, and Mage Arcadia is definitely not a place, so they can't really be one and the same without changing some details about one game's metaphysics or the other's. Not that there's anything wrong with doing so if it suits the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075628#post1075628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly, I just like the idea that the realms of Faerie are places even Archmages should think twice before interfering with (I know I know that's a minority position for a mage player, but whatever...),</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that the realm of Faerie has to be the same as the Supernal realm of the same name for this to be the case. In fact, I would say that it probably is the case under the setting's default assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075628#post1075628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and I kind of always thought Time and Fate would make excellent Archigenitors, so I personally loved the idea of the two Arcadias being the same because it gave me an excuse to say that Ruin and Prophet cannot find traction to be Archigenitors because of the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:53:34-07:00","id":1075654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075634#post1075634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ruin is about nihilism; making people think they can't pursue opportunities in front of them, out of cynicism borne of too many failures and suffering.<br /> The Prophet is about elitism; making people think that history can only be shaped by great leaders separate from the masses.<br /> <br /> The existence and doings of the True Fae seem to promote both of those concepts. They're majestic god-like beings who deny your life and steal your destiny from you. Which is why I think that Changeling!Arcadia is where the Ruin and the Prophet hold dominion.<br /> <br /> Now, this doesn't mean the True Fae are servants of the Exarchs, not any more than every clergy of established religions being servants of the Father. The relation between the Fallen and the Supernal is more than simple causality. But still, this would indeed make even archmages think twice about messing with the Gentry and their homeland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I love that very much! I actually pictured it more like a sort of rivalry, with neither side gaining traction against the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075633#post1075633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I'm pretty sure it was explicitly answered in Imperial Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Old Gods of Thistle bit? I scoured that book for ideas and it is still on the fence about it\u2014it was in the category of \u201cstuff you could get to via supernal but you\u2019re not sure what the hell it is\u201d.<br /> <br /> I found Equinox Road to be a lot more informative, for both separation and integration of the Arcadias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075636#post1075636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, though, I don't think word-of-author is needed to establish that the two Arcadias cannot be the same. One is a place where stories are sentient and the other is a collection of symbols and concepts related to fate and time. They can certainly be connected, the emanation realm idea being one example of how that might work, bur Changeling Arcadia is definitely a place, and Mage Arcadia is definitely not a place, so they can't really be one and the same without changing some details about one game's metaphysics or the other's. Not that there's anything wrong with doing so if it suits the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know that the realm of Faerie has to be the same as the Supernal realm of the same name for this to be the case. In fact, I would say that it probably is the case under the setting's default assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally understand where you are coming from, especially it goes to show more how Mage\u2019s setting is more about perspective and philosophy than facts, but I actually still kinda disagree! But only because the nature of Lustrums sort of creates \u201cplaces\u201d, so in my view the only thing that would be needed is for the existence of the Gentry as \u201cliving lustrums\u201d to be as passable an explanation as \u201cliving stories.\u201d Reading Equinox Road sort of made the \u201csupernal travel\u201d sections in Imperial Mysteries seem uncannily similar.<br /> <br /> But that just might be me though\u2014in my personal cosmology for Mage, I see Mages getting nowhere against the Exarchs on account of them thinking their understanding of the cosmos trumps that of other supernatural creatures, but that other supernatural templates are actually paradoxically more capable of understanding and explaining the supernal than mages are\u2014except for the detail of not being able to see or sense it.<br /> Which makes Mages stuck between a rock and a hard place.<br /> I suppose I should have looked closer at the publication dates for Equinox Road and Imperial Mysteries though\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019ll have to hope that this tangent only shows OP just how much more potential and possibilities they have to work with.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:40:58-07:00","id":1075665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075634#post1075634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ruin is about nihilism; making people think they can't pursue opportunities in front of them, out of cynicism borne of too many failures and suffering.<br /> The Prophet is about elitism; making people think that history can only be shaped by great leaders separate from the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that the Exarchs aren't <i>just</i> the most popular interpretations; they are <i>every</i> way that their Arcanum's symbolism can be twisted to dehumanize and enslave humanity. Case in point: The Chancellor is certainly all about making everything and everyone into a commodity that can be bought and sold, but it's also about restricting access to material goods in a more general sense, as happens with drug patents (to borrow Dave's example).<br /> <br /> The Prophet is all about Great Man History, but it's also likely about restriction of access to knowledge of history as well. Not just in the Orwellian &quot;We've always been at war with Eastasia!&quot; sense, but in creating false narratives that change the meaning of a historical event or shape the context in which people think of things. Consider, for example, Labour Day; a day created for the sake of the organized labour movement and to give workers a day to meet and organize and the public a chance to appreciate all that organized workers' movements have done.<br /> <br /> Don't exactly see much of that, now, do you? It's all &quot;Have a barbecue this Labour Day weekend!&quot;, with complete apathy towards why the day exists in the first place. I can't help but imagine the Prophet laughs every time such an ad plays.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:03:31-07:00","id":1075691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074562-new-mage-storyteller?p=1075665#post1075665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worth noting that the Exarchs aren't <i>just</i> the most popular interpretations; they are <i>every</i> way that their Arcanum's symbolism can be twisted to dehumanize and enslave humanity. Case in point: The Chancellor is certainly all about making everything and everyone into a commodity that can be bought and sold, but it's also about restricting access to material goods in a more general sense, as happens with drug patents (to borrow Dave's example).<br /> <br /> The Prophet is all about Great Man History, but it's also likely about restriction of access to knowledge of history as well. Not just in the Orwellian &quot;We've always been at war with Eastasia!&quot; sense, but in creating false narratives that change the meaning of a historical event or shape the context in which people think of things. Consider, for example, Labour Day; a day created for the sake of the organized labour movement and to give workers a day to meet and organize and the public a chance to appreciate all that organized workers' movements have done.<br /> <br /> Don't exactly see much of that, now, do you? It's all &quot;Have a barbecue this Labour Day weekend!&quot;, with complete apathy towards why the day exists in the first place. I can't help but imagine the Prophet laughs every time such an ad plays.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said. I just love how 2e emphasizes that the Exarchs are <i>right there</i>, in front of us, even in the most mundane and prosaic things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:17:24-07:00","id":1077083,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your input ! It's been really helpfull for me, i feel like i better understand the supernal now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}